      <div type="clause" n="5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ we cwædon be ciricbryce: gif he ful wære on ðam ðryfealdan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IIAs_5.lnote.oe.14"/> ordale, bete be þam þe sio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IIAs_5.lnote.oe.15"/> dómboc secge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>[Be<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IIAs_5.lnote.oe.24"/> cyricbryce.] And we cwædon be cyricbryce: gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_5.lnote.oe.1"/> he fúl wære on ða<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_5.lnote.oe.3"/></hi> ðryfealdan ordale, [bete<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#IIAs_5.lnote.oe.26"/>] be ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_5.lnote.oe.3"/> ðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#IIAs_5.lnote.oe.27"/> seo dómboc secge.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#IIAs_5.lnote.oe.28"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-so"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>Be cyricbryce. We cwædon be cyricbryce: gif he ful wære on ðam þreofealdum ordale, bete be ðam þe seo domboc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_5.lnote.oe.8"/> sæcge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#IIAs_5.lnote.oe.27-2"/><pb n="153" ed="#liebermann"/>Et de infracturis ecclesiarum: si quis reus appareat in triplici ordalio, emendetur sicut iudicialis liber dicit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="5" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="130" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be cyricbryce.]<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IIAs_5.attnote.fn.10"/> ⁊ we cwædon be ciricbryce: gif he ful wære on ðam þryfealdan<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#IIAs_5.attnote.fn.11"/> ordale, bete be þam þe sio dómboc secge.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="153" ed="#liebermann"/>(Von Einbruch in Kirchen. <hi rend="italic">B So</hi>) Und wir bestimmten über Einbruch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_5.lnote.de.1"/> in Kirchen, wenn der [Missethäter] überführt wird im dreifachen Ordal, büsse er gemäss dem, was das Gesetzbuch besagt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of breaking into churches. B So) And we determined concerning breaking into churches: if the [offender] is convicted in the threefold ordeal, let him pay compensation according to what the law-book says.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="131" ed="#attenborough"/>And we have declared with regard to breaking into a church—if he [who is accused of doing so] is found guilty in the threefold ordeal<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_5.attnote.n.1"/>, he shall pay such compensation for it as the written law declares<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_5.attnote.n.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="419" ed="#whitelock"/>And we have pronounced concerning breaking into a church; if he [who is accused] be convicted at the three-fold ordeal, he is to pay according to what the law-book<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_5.whinote.n.3"/> says.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="153"><ref target="clause:Af_6">Af 6</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. Af. 6</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="419"><label>refers to</label> <ref target="clause:Af_6">Af 6</ref> <quote>The reference in this chapter is to Alfred 6.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="148"><label>alludes to (implied referent)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_6">Af 6</ref> <quote>bete be þam þe sio dómboc segce). The implied referent seems to be Alfred §7, though no reference to the ordeal is made here</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">‘bete’ was added in the margin of B in the 16th century. Liebermann compares Af 6.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_5.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Ld; Raum für Rubrik B</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so Ld; space for a rubric B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_5.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_5.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_5.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. am Rande B</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in the margin in the 16th cent. B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_5.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_5.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sæcge <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sæcge Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_5.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">und</hi> an <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y and an on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_5.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> seo</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to seo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_5.lnote.oe.27-2" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">De infracturis ęcclesiarum <hi rend="italic">Rubrik MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">De infracturis ęcclesiarum rubric MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_5.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-bót</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-bót</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_5.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">So Schmid, Toller 155 b. Auch in den Compositis <hi rend="italic">burg-, eodor-, husbryce</hi> bedeutet <hi rend="italic">-bryce</hi> gewaltsames Eindringen. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Kirchenraub 5; Ordal 33 c. Price-Thorpe verstanden blosse ‘Privilegverletzung’; aber für Friedensbruch braucht ECf 6 u. a. andere Ausdrücke, z. B. <hi rend="italic">griðbryce</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">So Schmid, Toller 155 b. In the compounds <hi rend="italic">burg-, eodor-, husbryce</hi> too, <hi rend="italic">-bryce</hi> means forcible entry. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Kirchenraub 5; Ordal 33 c. Price-Thorpe understood mere ‘violation of privilege’; but for breach of the peace ECf 6 and other texts use other expressions, e.g. <hi rend="italic">griðbryce</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_5.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. note to Ine, cap. 37.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_5.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. Alf. cap. 6; I Wm. cap. 15; Edw. Conf. cap. 6.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_5.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>cyricbryce</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">B, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_5.attnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>þryfealdan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þreofealdum</hi>. So.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IIAs_5.whinote.n.3" n="3" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">419</biblScope></bibl><label>law-book</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The laws of Alfred, with those of Ine as an appendix. The reference in this chapter is to Alfred 6.</seg></note>
      </div>
